build/experiments/rocket-hyperlinux-20260928/hyper-linux/src.

Imported and adapted blocks (each marked "imported from HL <file>" in the source):
  - src/net/unixaddr.c, abstract_dir() and abstract_to_path(): the per-user private directory and the
    FNV-1a mapping of an abstract AF_UNIX name to a socket file of HL syscall_net.c (hl_abstract_dir,
    abstract_to_path). Adapted: LKD directory name, no process-wide lock table (a flock'ed lock file per
    name and a name file for getsockname/getpeername are kept instead).

The other files of src/net were written for LKD; their design follows the HL modules syscall_net.c,
syscall_poll.c, syscall_fd.c and syscall_inotify.c (read, not copied): the sockaddr/option/flag translation
tables come from core (src/core/xlate.c), epoll over kqueue with EV_CLEAR and EV_ONESHOT follows
syscall_poll.c, the inotify subset follows the limits listed in the header of src/net/inotify.c.
